NNAAMMEE
     du - summarize disk usage

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     dduu [-aa] [-ss] [_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y ...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     For each named _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y, dduu walks the directory tree rooted
     there and prints, in 512-byte blocks, the space used by each
     subdirectory (as a running subtotal, most deeply nested
     first), followed by the grand total for _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y itself.
     If no _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y is given, dduu reports on the current direc-
     tory.  If a named argument is a plain file rather than a
     directory, dduu prints its size and nothing else.

     -aa   Also print a line for every plain file, not just for
          directories.

     -ss   Print only the single grand total for each named _d_i_r_e_c-
          _t_o_r_y (or file); suppresses the per-subdirectory and, if
          -aa was also given, per-file lines.

     dduu counts a file that has more than one link to it only
     once, using an internal table of up to 500 (device, i-num-
     ber) pairs already seen; if a tree contains more distinct
     multiply-linked files than that, dduu warns and the excess
     ones are counted more than once.

     Because each level of directory recursion holds a file
     descriptor and some stack, a directory tree nested more than
     12 levels deep is finished by a forked child process rather
     than by further recursion in the same process; this is nor-
     mal and not reported as an error.

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     dduu prints a warning and skips (counting it as zero blocks)
     any directory it cannot open or a directory entry it cannot
     ssttaatt(), and a ``directory structure too deep to traverse''
     warning if a path name grows too long to hold, or if forking
     to continue a deeply nested tree fails.  None of these war-
     nings changes the exit status, which is 0 unless dduu was
     given an unrecognized option.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     ddff, ffiinndd

NNOOTTEESS
     dduu does not account for indirect blocks or other file-system
     overhead, so its totals can under-report the space a tree
     actually occupies on a device.
